  "This is the `docker-compose.yml` the agent runs (the `.env` file supplies the values). The collector image is pinned; when a newer OneUptime release bumps the pin, download both files again before pulling:":
    "Dit is de `docker-compose.yml` die de agent draait (het `.env`-bestand levert de waarden). De collector-image is vastgezet; wanneer een nieuwere OneUptime-release de vastgezette versie ophoogt, download je beide bestanden opnieuw voordat je pullt:",
  "And the full `otel-collector-config.yaml`. The `resource` processor stamps the `vmware.vcenter.name` attribute that registers the vCenter in OneUptime and that every VMware page, monitor and alert template scopes on — keep it in place if you customize the config. The `batch` processor deliberately has no `send_batch_max_size`: OneUptime reads a whole collection per request to sum inventory counts and infer VM power state, so a collection must never be split across exports:":
    "En de volledige `otel-collector-config.yaml`. De `resource`-processor zet het attribuut `vmware.vcenter.name` op de data; dat registreert de vCenter in OneUptime, en elke VMware-pagina, elke monitor en elk waarschuwingssjabloon is erop afgebakend — laat het staan als je de configuratie aanpast. De `batch`-processor heeft bewust geen `send_batch_max_size`: OneUptime leest per verzoek een hele verzameling om inventaristellingen op te tellen en de energiestatus van VM's af te leiden, dus een verzameling mag nooit over meerdere exports verdeeld worden:",
  "Every `VCENTER_COLLECTION_INTERVAL` the receiver walks the full vSphere inventory and emits one OpenTelemetry resource per object. Identity lives in **resource attributes** — `vcenter.datacenter.name`, `vcenter.cluster.name`, `vcenter.host.name`, `vcenter.vm.name` / `vcenter.vm.id`, `vcenter.datastore.name`, `vcenter.resource_pool.name` / `vcenter.resource_pool.inventory_path` — and the agent adds `vmware.vcenter.name` on top so OneUptime can route everything to your vCenter.":
    "Elke `VCENTER_COLLECTION_INTERVAL` loopt de receiver de hele vSphere-inventaris af en zendt per object één OpenTelemetry-resource uit. De identiteit zit in **resource-attributen** — `vcenter.datacenter.name`, `vcenter.cluster.name`, `vcenter.host.name`, `vcenter.vm.name` / `vcenter.vm.id`, `vcenter.datastore.name`, `vcenter.resource_pool.name` / `vcenter.resource_pool.inventory_path` — en de agent voegt daar `vmware.vcenter.name` aan toe, zodat OneUptime alles naar je vCenter kan leiden.",
  "| vSphere object | Identity (resource attributes) | Metrics |":
    "| vSphere-object | Identiteit (resource-attributen) | Metrics |",
  "| **Datacenter** | `vcenter.datacenter.name` | `vcenter.datacenter.cluster.count{status}`, `.host.count{status,power_state}`, `.vm.count{status,power_state}`, `.datastore.count`, `.disk.space{disk_state}`, `.cpu.limit`, `.memory.limit` |":
    "| **Datacenter** | alleen `vcenter.datacenter.name` | `vcenter.datacenter.cluster.count{status}`, `.host.count{status,power_state}`, `.vm.count{status,power_state}`, `.datastore.count`, `.disk.space{disk_state}`, `.cpu.limit`, `.memory.limit` |",
  "| **Cluster** | + `vcenter.cluster.name` | `vcenter.cluster.cpu.effective`, `.cpu.limit`, `.memory.effective`, `.memory.limit`, `.host.count{effective}`, `.vm.count{power_state}`, `.vm_template.count`, `vcenter.cluster.vsan.*` |":
    "| **Cluster** | plus `vcenter.cluster.name` | `vcenter.cluster.cpu.effective`, `.cpu.limit`, `.memory.effective`, `.memory.limit`, `.host.count{effective}`, `.vm.count{power_state}`, `.vm_template.count`, `vcenter.cluster.vsan.*` |",
  "| **ESXi host** | + `vcenter.host.name` (and `vcenter.cluster.name` when clustered) | `vcenter.host.cpu.usage` / `.capacity` / `.utilization` / `.reserved`, `.memory.usage` / `.utilization` / `.capacity`, `.disk.latency.avg` / `.latency.max` / `.throughput`, `.network.usage` / `.throughput` / `.packet.rate` / `.packet.drop.rate` / `.packet.error.rate`, `vcenter.host.vsan.*` |":
    "| **ESXi-host** | plus `vcenter.host.name` (en `vcenter.cluster.name` als hij in een cluster zit) | `vcenter.host.cpu.usage` / `.capacity` / `.utilization` / `.reserved`, `.memory.usage` / `.utilization` / `.capacity`, `.disk.latency.avg` / `.latency.max` / `.throughput`, `.network.usage` / `.throughput` / `.packet.rate` / `.packet.drop.rate` / `.packet.error.rate`, `vcenter.host.vsan.*` |",
  "| **Virtual machine** | + `vcenter.host.name`, `vcenter.vm.name`, `vcenter.vm.id` (instance UUID); `vcenter.resource_pool.*` or `vcenter.virtual_app.*` | `vcenter.vm.disk.usage{disk_state}`, `.disk.utilization`, `.memory.usage` / `.utilization` / `.ballooned` / `.swapped` / `.swapped_ssd`; **powered-on VMs only:** `.cpu.usage`, `.cpu.readiness`, `.cpu.utilization`, `.disk.latency.*` / `.throughput`, `.network.*`, `vcenter.vm.vsan.*` |":
    "| **Virtuele machine** | plus `vcenter.host.name`, `vcenter.vm.name`, `vcenter.vm.id` (instantie-UUID); `vcenter.resource_pool.*` of `vcenter.virtual_app.*` | `vcenter.vm.disk.usage{disk_state}`, `.disk.utilization`, `.memory.usage` / `.utilization` / `.ballooned` / `.swapped` / `.swapped_ssd`; **alleen ingeschakelde VM's:** `.cpu.usage`, `.cpu.readiness`, `.cpu.utilization`, `.disk.latency.*` / `.throughput`, `.network.*`, `vcenter.vm.vsan.*` |",
  "| **VM template** | `vcenter.vm_template.name`, `vcenter.vm_template.id` | `vcenter.vm.disk.usage{disk_state}` only |":
    "| **VM-sjabloon** | `vcenter.vm_template.name`, `vcenter.vm_template.id` | alleen `vcenter.vm.disk.usage{disk_state}` |",
